## Scope: text only

This checkpoint is multimodal; **this target is the language model only.** The vision tower is out of scope — do not port it, do not write a catalog entry for it, and do not treat its absence as a gap to close.

Two consequences that are easy to get wrong:

- **The weight loader must ignore the vision tensors rather than fail on them.** They are present in the checkpoint and always will be. A loader that asserts every tensor was consumed will fail on a correct target.
- **Gate it with text-only prompts.** An image prompt against a text-only target is a wrong question, and the error it raises is not a defect.
